[SPEAKER_00]: Whenever it was done, it was relevant because it was done presently.

191
00:12:48,534 --> 00:12:49,655
[SPEAKER_00]: And that's why it's a gateway.

192
00:12:49,855 --> 00:12:57,480
[SPEAKER_00]: Doesn't matter when... Like, that which didn't come through the gateway, lost to reversion, doesn't matter where it is, unless it's at the gateway.

193
00:12:58,656 --> 00:12:59,657
[SPEAKER_00]: So, that's the whole point.

194
00:12:59,697 --> 00:13:05,683
[SPEAKER_00]: The simile of the town, like, with big walls around, with only one way in or out.

195
00:13:06,324 --> 00:13:07,725
[SPEAKER_00]: And the wise man recognizes that.

196
00:13:07,765 --> 00:13:14,372
[SPEAKER_00]: So, he doesn't have to go and chase people that cause lust, or people that cause ill will, and police them.

197
00:13:14,572 --> 00:13:19,237
[SPEAKER_00]: All he needs to do, I just need to stay at the gateway, and not let them in, and there will be no trouble in the town.

198
00:13:20,708 --> 00:13:26,812
[SPEAKER_00]: When they are not at the gateway, entering the town, I don't care where they are and what they do, and when they turn up.

199
00:13:27,372 --> 00:13:29,253
[SPEAKER_00]: All I care is protecting the gateway.

200
00:13:31,735 --> 00:13:34,016
[SPEAKER_00]: And that gateway is not a random chance.

201
00:13:34,837 --> 00:13:35,737
[SPEAKER_00]: It's not a mistake.

202
00:13:36,378 --> 00:13:38,339
[SPEAKER_00]: It's not a momentary slip of mindfulness.

203
00:13:38,759 --> 00:13:41,961
[SPEAKER_00]: It's always intentional choice to open it.

204
00:13:42,582 --> 00:13:42,842
[SPEAKER_00]: Hence,

205
00:13:44,323 --> 00:13:50,644
[SPEAKER_00]: Literally, the entire dhamma boils down to one instruction that the Buddha gave often to numerous monks and nuns.

206
00:13:51,384 --> 00:13:53,365
[SPEAKER_00]: Whatever you know it's wholesome, do it.

207
00:13:54,125 --> 00:13:57,525
[SPEAKER_00]: Whenever you know it's rooted in unwholesome, don't do it.

208
00:13:58,585 --> 00:14:01,486
[SPEAKER_00]: Not like pray that it will come your way or something.

209
00:14:01,546 --> 00:14:01,686
[SPEAKER_00]: No.

210
00:14:01,906 --> 00:14:03,366
[SPEAKER_00]: Do it or don't do it.

211
00:14:03,946 --> 00:14:05,026
[SPEAKER_00]: It's a matter of choice.

212
00:14:05,927 --> 00:14:13,528
[SPEAKER_00]: So, if you cultivate the right choices sufficiently enough, you'll get to understand and uproot the nature of lust, aversion, delusion and distraction.

213
00:14:14,506 --> 00:14:19,011
[SPEAKER_00]: You get to fully discern the gateway and be unable to lose the sight of it.

214
00:14:21,074 --> 00:14:22,816
[SPEAKER_00]: That's why Arahant is always mindful.

215
00:14:22,996 --> 00:14:25,399
[SPEAKER_00]: Not because he's always, I'm at the gateway, I'm at the gateway.

216
00:14:25,439 --> 00:14:29,463
[SPEAKER_00]: No, it's because he fully, proficiently developed himself in regard to he cannot not see it anymore.

217
00:14:29,864 --> 00:14:31,145
[SPEAKER_00]: He cannot even ignore it anymore.

218
00:14:31,185 --> 00:14:32,467
[SPEAKER_00]: Because it's impossible to ignore.

219
00:14:34,142 --> 00:14:40,947
[SPEAKER_00]: Like, even when you think you're ignoring things, you're only ignoring, pretty much, the responsibility for your choices.

220
00:14:41,448 --> 00:14:46,712
[SPEAKER_00]: But you... you wouldn't be able to make choices, even in a state of half-awareness that most people live in.

221
00:14:47,953 --> 00:14:48,734
[SPEAKER_00]: They're choices.

222
00:14:48,754 --> 00:14:49,955
[SPEAKER_00]: There's... you're still aware of them.

223
00:14:50,649 --> 00:14:57,513
[SPEAKER_00]: So, that whole delusion and ignoring and unawareness, it's not this mystical non-existence or some mystery that you don't know.

224
00:14:57,974 --> 00:15:00,355
[SPEAKER_00]: It's you actively ignoring part of the picture.

225
00:15:00,415 --> 00:15:02,637
[SPEAKER_00]: Ignoring your responsibility for opening the gate.

226
00:15:03,397 --> 00:15:06,379
[SPEAKER_00]: Ignoring your responsibility for letting people in or trying to chase them out.

227
00:15:06,479 --> 00:15:07,560
[SPEAKER_00]: Either way, opening the door.

228
00:15:09,181 --> 00:15:11,982
[SPEAKER_00]: But either way, you cannot ignore it for as long as you're alive.

229
00:15:13,443 --> 00:15:15,525
[SPEAKER_00]: Because that's what being alive is.

230
00:15:15,605 --> 00:15:16,245
[SPEAKER_00]: Being conscious.

231
00:15:16,825 --> 00:15:17,366
[SPEAKER_00]: Being aware.

232
00:15:19,755 --> 00:15:22,976
[SPEAKER_00]: So, when people say, I'll come back to the present moment, you have no choice about it.

233
00:15:23,496 --> 00:15:27,137
[SPEAKER_00]: You are in the present moment whether you want or not.

234
00:15:27,197 --> 00:15:30,918
[SPEAKER_00]: But what you should do is stop ignoring responsibility for the present moment.

235
00:15:31,939 --> 00:15:38,561
[SPEAKER_00]: Stop ignoring that fundamentally it's your choice that has all these various symptoms later on arising and bothering you.

236
00:15:39,101 --> 00:15:44,283
[SPEAKER_00]: Choice of lust, choice of ill-will, choice of ignoring responsibility, delusion.

237
00:15:45,763 --> 00:15:48,304
[SPEAKER_00]: Choice of oblivion, choice of carelessness.

238
00:15:49,664 --> 00:16:01,312
[SPEAKER_00]: And as we began this talk, none of these things would manifest unless you acted out of them and unless you keep acting out of them by body, speech and mind.

239
00:16:01,492 --> 00:16:05,734
[SPEAKER_00]: So, yeah, protect the behavior of your body, of your speech and your mind.

240
00:16:06,355 --> 00:16:08,576
[SPEAKER_00]: And the Bodhisattva, the skillful monk practices like this.

241
00:16:09,137 --> 00:16:09,617
[SPEAKER_00]: He's gonna...

242
00:16:10,600 --> 00:16:34,048
[SPEAKER_00]: You know, he will restrain his behavior, he'll restrain his speech, then he's gonna have still like thoughts of cruelty, coarse sensuality arise for him, but he sustains his practice, these thoughts will diminish, then he's gonna have subtler thoughts, you know, like subtler annoyances, thoughts of his clan, country, reputation, kind of broader, subtler things, then that will subside.

243
00:16:34,849 --> 00:16:37,850
[SPEAKER_00]: And then, he's just gonna have thoughts of purity of dhamma.

244
00:16:38,795 --> 00:16:39,896
[SPEAKER_00]: Things as they are, literally.

245
00:16:40,056 --> 00:16:43,598
[SPEAKER_00]: Like, in seen just the seen, in heard just the heard, in thought just the thought.

246
00:16:44,698 --> 00:16:48,441
[SPEAKER_00]: So, no more corruption, no more confusion about the gateway.

247
00:16:49,321 --> 00:16:52,823
[SPEAKER_00]: But again, that doesn't happen magically.

248
00:16:52,963 --> 00:16:59,767
[SPEAKER_00]: He clearly understood what not to be done, and then he kept a watchful eye, peripherally, on things that are bad to be done.

249
00:17:00,427 --> 00:17:02,128
[SPEAKER_00]: And then, didn't do them if they're unwholesome.

250
00:17:02,148 --> 00:17:04,690
[SPEAKER_00]: If they're wholesome, kept an eye on them and allowed them to be done.

251
00:17:08,130 --> 00:17:11,091
[SPEAKER_00]: But not just physically, but verbally and mentally.

252
00:17:12,152 --> 00:17:20,575
[SPEAKER_00]: That's why often the Buddha would, you know, give all those instructions about the speech, and careless speech, and malicious speech, and even if it's not coarsely bad speech, pointless speech.

253
00:17:21,475 --> 00:17:23,396
[SPEAKER_00]: Are you just chit-chatting for whatever reason?

254
00:17:24,077 --> 00:17:32,060
[SPEAKER_00]: Means you are now choosing to maintain the kind of, like, because you cannot engage in a careless chit-chat,

255
00:17:33,010 --> 00:17:38,793
[SPEAKER_00]: verbally, without that implying a certain obliviousness on the level of your mind.

256
00:17:40,214 --> 00:17:43,475
[SPEAKER_00]: A certain, like, careless, pointless choice of a distraction.

257
00:17:46,617 --> 00:17:48,778
[SPEAKER_00]: So, and that's where you want to arrive ultimately.

258
00:17:49,058 --> 00:17:53,220
[SPEAKER_00]: The clarity of your thoughts in regard to presently enduring pressure of any hindrance.

259
00:17:54,101 --> 00:17:59,043
[SPEAKER_00]: Whether it's sensuality, ill will, restlessness, doubt, remorse, sluggishness, doesn't matter.

260
00:18:00,988 --> 00:18:07,452
[SPEAKER_00]: It's rooted in the mind, but you will not see that for as long as you physically immediately act out of it, for as long as you verbally act out of it.

261
00:18:09,314 --> 00:18:14,817
[SPEAKER_00]: But if you don't, you get to see that, oh, look, I'm cultivating such and such thoughts when this hindrance is present.

262
00:18:14,997 --> 00:18:26,145
[SPEAKER_00]: I am choosing, literally, I am choosing, when these things are present, I make a choice for these thoughts to start to move.

263
00:18:27,833 --> 00:18:30,635
[SPEAKER_00]: So, what if I just choose not to do that?

264
00:18:31,236 --> 00:18:37,220
[SPEAKER_00]: Not like I choose to get rid of this, because you can't, so you endure it, but I choose to not entertain such and such thoughts.

265
00:18:39,762 --> 00:18:46,086
[SPEAKER_00]: And then you sustain the choice for which recognition of that thing enduring there is still necessary.

266
00:18:46,206 --> 00:18:46,767
[SPEAKER_00]: It's implicit.

267
00:18:47,487 --> 00:18:49,989
[SPEAKER_00]: So, you cannot not be mindful with such practice.

268
00:18:51,090 --> 00:18:52,031
[SPEAKER_01]: That's the meditation.

269
00:18:52,071 --> 00:18:53,171
[SPEAKER_00]: That's the... That's samādhi.

270
00:18:53,352 --> 00:18:54,572
[SPEAKER_00]: That's the meditation.

271
00:18:54,632 --> 00:18:56,354
[SPEAKER_00]: Being able to sustain it, to compose it.

272
00:18:57,156 --> 00:18:58,918
[SPEAKER_00]: Compose it the right way and sustain it.

273
00:18:59,358 --> 00:19:00,359
[SPEAKER_00]: Maintain it in the being.

274
00:19:00,499 --> 00:19:00,959
[SPEAKER_00]: Bhāvanam.

275
00:19:02,781 --> 00:19:05,904
[SPEAKER_01]: The samādhi of patience, of patient endurance.

276
00:19:05,944 --> 00:19:07,445
[SPEAKER_00]: Well, yeah, it's one of the factors.

277
00:19:10,628 --> 00:19:15,032
[SPEAKER_00]: If you practice patience rightly, you will develop samādhi.

278
00:19:15,072 --> 00:19:18,855
[SPEAKER_00]: Patience in regard to right things, not patience in regard to, you know, enduring ants biting me.

279
00:19:19,296 --> 00:19:19,516
[SPEAKER_00]: Why?

280
00:19:19,976 --> 00:19:20,957
[SPEAKER_00]: What's the reason for it?

281
00:19:24,375 --> 00:19:33,780
[SPEAKER_00]: But yeah, enduring the pressure of the certain choices, that you know are unwholesome, and you don't do, throughout the day, from the moment you wake up, to the moment you go to bed.

282
00:19:34,040 --> 00:19:46,487
[SPEAKER_00]: And we said that before, a useful practice would be at the end of the day, not as a sort of mantra or something, just sit down and see, have there been instances during the day, where you actually acted out of things, that should have not been acted out.

283
00:19:47,609 --> 00:19:48,850
[SPEAKER_00]: When you acted out of lust, your will.

284
00:19:49,891 --> 00:19:52,233
[SPEAKER_00]: And if you remember, yes, I did such...

285
00:19:52,273 --> 00:19:54,254
[SPEAKER_00]: I said such and such thing in the morning, it was careless.

286
00:19:55,335 --> 00:19:59,678
[SPEAKER_00]: Don't go through this, like, psychotherapy motions of, I will ask forgiveness and stuff.

287
00:19:59,978 --> 00:20:01,820
[SPEAKER_00]: I mean, you do it, whatever, but it's pointless.

288
00:20:02,360 --> 00:20:10,606
[SPEAKER_00]: But what you want to do, that it's not pointless, is recognize there and then, re-discern the gateway, because of which you've done such a thing in the morning.

289
00:20:11,087 --> 00:20:12,468
[SPEAKER_00]: That's the way to deal with it.

290
00:20:13,946 --> 00:20:15,187
[SPEAKER_01]: Remember your responsibility.

291
00:20:15,207 --> 00:20:16,227
[SPEAKER_00]: Remember your responsibility.

292
00:20:16,307 --> 00:20:17,307
[SPEAKER_00]: So, I'll never do that again.

293
00:20:17,367 --> 00:20:18,988
[SPEAKER_00]: I don't know if I'm going to do it again or not.

294
00:20:19,448 --> 00:20:21,729
[SPEAKER_00]: But how do I do it whenever I do do it?

295
00:20:22,369 --> 00:20:23,550
[SPEAKER_00]: By losing the sight of the gateway.

296
00:20:23,590 --> 00:20:32,934
[SPEAKER_00]: Like, oh, this gateway that now I'm losing the sight of because I'm so obsessed with this remorse and making determination that I will never make this mistake again.

297
00:20:33,514 --> 00:20:36,735
[SPEAKER_00]: And yet, you're doing it right there and then, ignoring the gateway.

298
00:20:38,596 --> 00:20:39,076
[SPEAKER_01]: And that's it.

